KZ3 patch 1140 (SPU pass 117): the kernel threads of chosen SPURS instances (KZ3_SPU_PCORES_SPURS, comma-separated name
prefixes, unset = "LoPrio", the audio SPU) are restricted to the performance cores like the spu_async_thread job threads
(patch 1136). Pass 117 measured the LoPrio kernel thread (Amadeus/BrB audio) at 620-760 ms/s on a P-core in K2 and the
scheduler leaving it on the E-cores for 10-20 s at a time at 1000 ms/s (saturated): audio units fell below real time and
port 0 got 100-560 holes per 10 s, the in-level stutter. kz3_spu_thread_sched() now returns whether it restricted the
thread. KZ3_SPU_PCORES=0 also turns this off. Upstream candidate (the mechanism; the default name is KZ3's).

--- a/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c
+++ b/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c
@@ -2485,6 +2485,8 @@
             si->prefix, kt + 1, si->nthreads, si->ea, s_pm_off ? "DISABLED (PS3_NO_SPURS_PM)" : "enabled");
     fflush(stderr);
     if (kz3_wacct_on()) { char nm[40]; snprintf(nm, sizeof nm, "spurs-kern%d:%s", kt, si->prefix); kz3_wacct_name(nm); }
+    if (kz3_spurs_pcore_thread(si->prefix))   /* KZ3 patch 1140: the audio SPU (LoPrio) stays off the E-cores */
+        fprintf(stderr, "[spu-sched] SPURS \"%s\" kernel thread %d restricted to the performance cores (KZ3_SPU_PCORES_SPURS)\n", si->prefix, kt);
     if (!kz3_kern_old()) { kz3_spu_loop(si, kt, (int)s_pm_off); return 0; }   /* KZ3 patch 1074 */
 
     /* Instance change detector (SPURS_KERN_WATCH=1).
